  "_comment": "Curated tag vocabulary for the print catalogue. Marketplace tags in model.toml are written per platform (Printables allows only [a-z0-9]), so the same idea arrives as nosupports, no-supports and 'no supports'. The builder folds every spelling to a compact key (letters and digits only), then: `drop` removes keys that describe the workflow rather than the object, `aliases` maps a key to its canonical kebab-case tag, and any key left over becomes the most-hyphenated spelling seen in the data. `labels` overrides the display text for acronyms and brands; every other tag is shown as its words in sentence case.",
